      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:6:3:4",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) يَقُولُ أَيُّ قَاضٍ قَضَى بَيْنَ اثْنَيْنِ فَأَخْطَأَ سَقَطَ أَبْعَدَ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Sahl Bin Ziyad, from Muhammad Bin Isa, from Abu Abdullah Al Momin, from Muawiya Bin Wahab who said, ",
          "‘I heard Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘Whichever judge who judges between two, so he errs, falls from further than the sky’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. A number of our people have narrated from Sahl ibn Ziyad from Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from ‘Abd Allah al-Mu’min from Mu‘awiyah ibn Wahab who has narrated the following: “I once heard abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, saying, ‘Any judge who issues a judgment between the two and makes a mistake, he falls into a depth farther than the sky.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
